    esp32s3-eye: contest-2026 branch compatibility fixes.

    Three fixes needed to make the V5 ESP32-S3-EYE adaptation work cleanly
    on the dev-ai-contest-2026 branch (vs apache/nuttx where it was
    originally developed):

    1. arch/xtensa/src/common/xtensa_debug.c
       Handle BREAK / BREAK.N debug exceptions instead of looping forever.
       Without this, when contest-branch BSP code hits any 'break' assembly
       instruction (issued e.g. by some assert paths on idle CPU1), the
       debug exception handler classifies cause=0x08 as 'Unhandled' and
       returns with EPC unchanged, immediately re-executing the BREAK and
       flooding the console with thousands of 'Unhandled debug cause 0x8'
       lines per second. Fix: skip past the instruction (PC+=3 for BREAK,
       PC+=2 for BREAK.N) per Xtensa ISA Reference Manual.

    2. arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_i2s.c
       Add missing #include <nuttx/mutex.h> and <nuttx/semaphore.h>.
       The contest-branch i2s driver calls nxmutex_lock/unlock and
       nxsem_* but doesn't pull in the headers, so the inline-function
       versions never get defined and ld fails with 'undefined reference
       to nxmutex_lock' at link time when CONFIG_AUDIO_I2S=y.

