team 295 ESP32-S3 board options\"\n\nendif # ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM\n\n[contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/README.md]\n# ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 Board Port\n\n本目录提供 `ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8` 的最小 openvela 板级适配，并由\n作品仓 manifest 映射到：\n\n```text\nvendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_295_board\n```\n\n## Hardware baseline\n\n- Flash: 16 MB quad SPI Flash\n- PSRAM: 8 MB Octal PSRAM\n- Console: UART0, RX GPIO44 (module pin 36), TX GPIO43 (module pin 37)\n- Crystal: 40 MHz, consistent with the local ESP32-S3 board implementations\n\nFlash size is selected by `CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_ESP32S3WROOM1N16R8`.  PSRAM is\nenabled with `CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM` and `CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT`.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe initial port intentionally contains no LED, button, I2C, SPI, I2S, LCD,\ncamera, audio, or SDCard driver registration.  The available hardware notes\ndo not identify all attached devices and their electrical requirements well\nenough for safe initialization.\n\n## Build\n\nRun from the openvela workspace root:\n\n```bash\nCONTEST_REAL_ESPTOOL=\"$(command -v esptool.py)\" \\\nPATH=\"$PWD/contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/scripts:$PATH\" \\\nUSE_NXTMPDIR_ESP_REPO_DIRECTLY=y \\\n  ./build.sh vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_295_board/configs/nsh -j8\n```\n\n`scripts/esptool.py` adds `--use_segments` only to `elf2image`.  This is\nrequired by the locally installed esptool 4.12, which otherwise exceeds the\nESP32-S3 ROM segment limit when it expands the ELF by sections.\n\nHardware flashing and runtime validation require a physical board and serial\nconnection and are not implied by a successful build.\n"}],"is_error":false}
